## 7️⃣ TL;DR – One‑liner for a vector PMTiles source

```js
import * as pmtiles from 'pmtiles';
import maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';
maplibregl.addProtocol('pmtiles', new pmtiles.Protocol().tile);

new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: {
    version: 8,
    sources: {
      myPmtiles: { type: 'vector', url: 'pmtiles://https://cdn.example.com/tiles.pmtiles' }
    },
    layers: [{ id: 'water', type: 'fill', source: 'myPmtiles', 'source-layer': 'water', paint: { 'fill-color': '#a0c8f0' } }]
  },
  center: [0, 0],
  zoom: 2
});
```

That’s it—your `.pmtiles` file is now a fully functional MapLibre source! 🎉

