## 7️⃣ Full reference – the new `addProtocol` signature

```ts
/**
 * Register a custom protocol handler.
 *
 * @param name   Protocol name (e.g. "mytiles").
 * @param handler Function that receives the request parameters and an AbortSignal.
 *                It must return a Promise that resolves to either:
 *                - an ArrayBuffer / Uint8Array / string (the raw response body), or
 *                - an object { data, cacheControl?, expires?, headers? }.
 *
 * @example
 * maplibregl.addProtocol('mytiles', (params, abort) => {
 *   const url = buildUrlFromParams(params);
 *   return fetch(url, { signal: abort })
 *     .then(r => r.arrayBuffer())
 *     .then(buf => ({ data: buf, headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-protobuf' } }));
 * });
 */
addProtocol(name: string, handler: (params: ProtocolParams, abortSignal: AbortSignal) => Promise<ProtocolResponse | ArrayBuffer | Uint8Array | string>): void;
```

**`ProtocolParams`** (relevant fields):

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `url` | `string` | The URL *after* the protocol prefix (e.g. `https://example.com/tiles/{z}/{x}/{y}.pbf`). |
| `type` | `string` | Source type (`'vector'`, `'raster'`, `'raster-dem'`, `'glyphs'`, `'sprite'`, …). |
| `z`, `x`, `y` | `number` | Tile coordinates (only present for tile requests). |
| `headers` | `Record<string,string>` | Request headers MapLibre would send (e.g. `User-Agent`). |

**`ProtocolResponse`**:

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `data` | `ArrayBuffer` / `Uint8Array` / `string` | The response body. |
| `cacheControl` | `string` (optional) | e.g. `'public, max-age=31536000'`. |
| `expires` | `string` (optional) | HTTP‑date string. |
| `headers` | `Record<string,string>` (optional) | Additional response headers (e.g. `{'Content-Type': 'application/x-protobuf'}`). |

