## 7️⃣ Quick “Copy‑Paste” Starter Repo

If you want a ready‑made repo to clone and adapt:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/protomaps/pmtiles-demo.git
cd pmtiles-demo
# 1️⃣ Put your basemap.pmtiles in the `public/` folder (or upload to S3)
# 2️⃣ Deploy pg_tileserv (Docker) – see the repo’s README for a docker-compose file.
# 3️⃣ Run `npm install && npm start` – the page will load the static basemap and live bus layer.
```

The repo already contains the `pmtiles` protocol registration and a simple `setInterval` refresh loop.

---

### Final Verdict

> **Use PMTiles for the *static* part of your map (the basemap).**  
> **Use a *dynamic* vector‑tile endpoint (or GeoJSON polling) for the *bus positions* that change every 30 seconds.**  

That gives you the best of both worlds: a fast, CDN‑cached background map with zero‑ops hosting, plus truly live data that updates on the schedule you need. Happy mapping! 🚍🗺️
